# Documentation

## Scope and entry

Start at {{documentation_entry_relative_link}} and the project profile/native rules.
This procedure owns documentation, not product behavior, access or publication policy.

## Practical route

1. Find existing knowledge and its owner. Separate requirement, current implementation,
   proposal, history and verification. Update a suitable existing document before
   creating a new one; linking or justified no-document-impact can be sufficient.
2. Select kind/place/form from {{metadata_and_template_routes}}: current architecture,
   contract/reference, scenario, plan/decision, research, guide or verification.
   Use existing project directories; create no empty tree for completeness.
3. Before writing name finite paths and check dirty intersections. Copy only the
   selected payload, fill initial YAML, remove unnecessary sections and preserve
   project-specific decisions. Agent placeholders are not Obsidian variables.
4. Use ordinary relative Markdown links and stable IDs/anchors. Add one route from
   the nearest relevant entry; add an instruction trigger to its actual catalog.
   A link alone does not prove automatic agent loading.
5. For standalone architecture/contracts/scenarios include meaningful Mermaid
   relationships/states, or link a directly applicable parent diagram for an extracted
   fragment. State the arrows' meaning and distinguish proposed components.
   Check changed diagrams with an available renderer; report unrendered honestly.
6. Use illustrations only where they explain a task. Add alt/caption, version,
   language and origin; concepts are not implementation screenshots. Never acquire
   private data just for illustration. Text remains usable without images/Figma.
7. At substantive slice completion assess architecture, contracts, instructions,
   scenarios, examples/commands, guides and translations. The author updates affected
   owners in the same logical result; no impact permits a concise reason, not fake edits.

## Replacement, temporary outputs and views

Keep current knowledge at one stable address. A replacement declares `supersedes`,
old text becomes `superseded` with a human link and exact scope. Archive without
replacement records reason/origin and unresolved obligations; preserve historical
versions/evidence. Archiving never grants data deletion. Use {{archive_route}}.

Temporary TODOs, raw output and agent reports remain in the task's authorized area;
promote durable conclusions to their owner, not the whole run folder or chat history.
Do not create another tracker. Only remove your own temporary files when permitted.
Markdown is the source; optional catalog/Bases views select it, not a second wiki/DB.
Use {{views_route_or_explicit_no_views}} without requiring Obsidian to author/read docs.

## Checks and finish

Use {{verified_docs_check_command_or_explicit_unconfigured}} from
{{check_cwd_and_permitted_scope}}; do not invent a successful command.
Check properties/types/duplicate IDs, output-relative links, unresolved required fields,
source fidelity, diagram/image limits and real navigation. Capture raw exit/findings;
static success proves no runtime/visual behavior. Follow the project's acceptance/save
policy, including independent review when required, without appointing another layer;
preserve foreign hunks. Stop after the agreed result.

## Update this instruction

Revisit on schema, locations, template/check command, knowledge-owner or client-route
change. Synchronize accepted technical facts; policy changes need their actual owner.
